# ConverseIQ — Roo Code Project Rules & Architecture Context

You are working on **ConverseIQ**, an enterprise academic meeting intelligence platform designed for higher education institutions (Faculty, HOD, and Admin personas).

---

## 🏛️ 1. Technical Stack & Architecture

- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide React icons.
  - Path: `frontend/`
  - Dev server port: `3000` (`http://localhost:3000`)
  - API helper: `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` (`apiRequest`, `downloadFile`, `getAuthToken`)
- **Backend**: FastAPI v2, Python 3.12, SQLAlchemy async (`aiosqlite` / `asyncpg`), ReportLab (PDF generator), Pydantic v2.
  - Path: `backend_v2/`
  - Local backend port: `8001`
  - Live Render backend: `https://converseiq.onrender.com/api/v1`
  - Swagger docs: `https://converseiq.onrender.com/docs`
- **Live Deployment**:
  - Frontend: `https://converse-iq.vercel.app` (Vercel)
  - Backend: `https://converseiq.onrender.com` (Render)

---

## 🎨 2. Visual Identity & Design Tokens

Always adhere strictly to the **Soft Blue + Sage Green** design system. Do NOT introduce unrelated corporate purple, harsh blue, or beige colors.

### Core Color Palette:
- **Main Background**: `#F5FAF8` (Light) / `#0F1A15` (Dark)
- **Cards / Surfaces**: `#FFFFFF` (Light) / `#1A2B24` (Dark)
- **Primary Sage**: `#78A98F`
- **Deep Sage**: `#3F795F`
- **Light Sage**: `#D4E9DF` / `#243D33` (Dark)
- **Soft Blue**: `#B9DDE3`
- **Pale Blue**: `#E4F2F4` / `#1A3A3F` (Dark)
- **Deep Teal**: `#367C88`
- **Primary Text**: `#173A2C` (Light) / `#E8F0EC` (Dark)
- **Secondary Text**: `#667875` (Light) / `#8FA89C` (Dark)
- **Borders**: `#DCE7E2` (Light) / `#2D4A3E` (Dark)

### Dark Mode Support:
- Always pair classes: e.g. `bg-white dark:bg-[#1A2B24]`, `text-[#173A2C] dark:text-[#E8F0EC]`, `border-[#DCE7E2] dark:border-[#2D4A3E]`.
- Use `useTheme()` from `@/components/ThemeProvider` if programmatic theme detection is needed.

---

## 👥 3. Role-Based Portals & Routes

Never delete or break any of these 20 routes:

1. **Authentication**: `/login` (with demo quick-fill role switcher).
2. **Faculty Portal**:
   - `/dashboard` (Personal KPI cards, upcoming meetings, quick actions).
   - `/meetings` & `/meetings/[id]` (Meeting archive, speaker timeline, MoM view, PDF export).
   - `/live-meeting` (Speech waveform visualizer & live transcription).
   - `/mom` (Executive meeting summaries, decisions, PDF download).
   - `/action-items` (Interactive task tracker with strikethrough & priority badges).
   - `/schedule` (Meeting calendar & scheduling).
   - `/ai-assistant` (Grounded academic query assistant).
   - `/settings` (Profile, password change, data export, preferences).
3. **HOD Portal**:
   - `/hod/overview` (Department metrics & analytics).
   - `/hod/faculty` (Faculty workload & performance tracking).
   - `/hod/meetings` (Departmental meeting archive).
   - `/hod/action-tracker` (Branch-wide action item governance).
   - `/hod/schedule` (Departmental scheduling).
4. **Administration Suite**:
   - `/admin` (User management, department setup, system settings, real-time audit logs).

---

## ⚠️ 4. Strict Engineering Guardrails

1. **Zero Dummy Data Policy**:
   - Never inject hardcoded mock arrays like `const DUMMY_MEETINGS = [...]` into pages.
   - Always fetch from FastAPI endpoints via `apiRequest()`.
   - If the database returns 0 records, render a clean, polite empty state (e.g. *"No scheduled meetings found"*).
2. **Audit Logging**:
   - Every sensitive mutation on backend must call `log_audit_event(db, action, details, user_id, user_name)`.
3. **Compile Verification**:
   - After any frontend edit, run `npm --prefix frontend run build` to ensure 0 TypeScript or Next.js errors.
   - All 20 static pages must generate cleanly.
